# Security headers for Cloudflare Pages.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
# This file is copied verbatim into dist/ at build time and applied by the
# Cloudflare Pages edge. (Note: it is NOT applied by `astro preview`.) Vercel
# does not read _headers — vercel.json mirrors these headers for Vercel, and a
# test (tests/test.spec.js) asserts the two stay identical so they can't drift.
#
# Content-Security-Policy philosophy: lock down the high-risk directive
# (script-src) and stay permissive on the directives that commonly change as the
# site grows, so adding pages/images/fonts/styles doesn't silently break.
#   - script-src          first-party JS plus Cloudflare Web Analytics. Astro
#                         bundles framework islands (React/Svelte/etc.) as
#                         same-origin module scripts, so 'self' already covers
#                         them. static.cloudflareinsights.com is the beacon
#                         Cloudflare *injects at the edge* on Pages projects with
#                         Web Analytics enabled: it isn't in this repo, but it
#                         runs on every page, so the policy has to name it or the
#                         browser blocks it and logs a console error (which is
#                         what PageSpeed Insights flagged). Any other third-party
#                         script would likewise need its origin added here — and
#                         tests/test.spec.js will fail loudly if a page ever loads
#                         something this policy blocks.
#   - img/style/font      allow any https: source (+ data:) so new images, web
#                         fonts, or inline styles Just Work.
#   - connect-src         same-origin fetch/XHR, plus cloudflareinsights.com —
#                         where the beacon above POSTs its pageview. If you add
#                         client-side calls to a third-party API, widen this (the
#                         page-load test can't catch runtime fetches).
#   - form-action         the contact form posts to Formspree.
#
# Non-CSP notes:
#   - HSTS                Cloudflare injects its own HSTS at the edge (dashboard:
#                         SSL/TLS -> Edge Certificates -> HSTS), and that edge
#                         value overrides whatever this file sets. This file, the
#                         dashboard, and vercel.json must therefore all carry the
#                         same value (the test below enforces the repo half).
#                         That value is six months (15768000), Cloudflare's own
#                         recommended setting. It replaces the 30-day dashboard
#                         default, which left a device that hadn't visited in a
#                         month open to one SSL-strip attempt on its next
#                         plain-HTTP request. The `preload` token below is
#                         aspirational at this max-age: the HSTS preload list
#                         only accepts a domain at max-age >= 31536000 (one
#                         year), so actually submitting buckley.ca would mean
#                         raising this first. The token stays regardless because
#                         Cloudflare's Preload toggle is on and the edge emits it
#                         either way — this file mirrors what ships.
#                         *** Setting max-age here alone does nothing: set
#                         Cloudflare's dashboard HSTS to 6 months to match. ***
#                         Note the scope: pages are served from the apex
#                         (www 301s to buckley.ca), so includeSubDomains covers
#                         every *.buckley.ca host — the Google Workspace siblings
#                         (email, admin, docs, …) included. Those all speak HTTPS,
#                         and Cloudflare's edge injects this same value regardless
#                         of what ships here, so the scope is a fact to know rather
#                         than a knob this file turns. `preload` only advertises
#                         eligibility; it does not submit the domain to the
#                         preload list.
#   - Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy  severs window.opener between this page and any
#                         cross-origin page that opens it (or that it opens),
#                         closing tabnabbing and cross-window XS-Leaks. Safe here
#                         because nothing on the site relies on popup messaging.
#   Deliberately absent: Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy (would block the Cloudinary
#   background image) and Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy (would stop other origins
#   from embedding /og.png, which is the whole point of a social card).

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' https: data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https:; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; font-src 'self' https: data:; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; form-action 'self' https://formspree.io; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), browsing-topics=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15768000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  X-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies: none
